    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present No. 23 Mapas Road, a bright and well-proportioned three-bedroom semi-detached family home, ideally positioned in this highly sought-after and family-friendly location. Situated within walking distance of Dalkey Town Centre and DART station, and with a neighbourhood shop and créche close by, this property offers purchasers an excellent opportunity to create a stunning family home. The exceptionally private south-facing rear garden also provides excellent potential to extend, subject to the necessary planning permission.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, a dual-aspect living room opening through to the dining room with access to the rear garden, a kitchen/breakfast room overlooking the garden, a guest w.c. and an integral garage. Upstairs there are three generously sized bedrooms, a family bathroom and separate w.c. Stair's lead to a converted attic room with a skylight, an ideal space for a home office or additional storage.\n\nA standout feature is the wonderfully private south-facing rear garden. Laid mainly in lawn and bordered by mature flower beds, shrubs and trees, it provides the ideal space for outdoor dining, entertaining or simply enjoying the sunshine throughout the day. To the front - there is off-street parking together with the added benefit of the garage which could be converted to living accommodation as neighbouring properties have done.\n\nThe location itself needs little introduction, moments from Dalkey Town with renowned restaurants, bars and close to the scenic walks of Dun Laoghaire, Dalkey and Killiney Hill. The Dart station and bus service at Dalkey is close by, and there is excellent shopping at nearby Sandycove, Glasthule and Dun Laoghaire. There is easy access to the N11 and M50 which makes commuting to and from the city centre and nationwide very simple. There is an Aircoach servicing the airport frequently at Fitzpatrick's Castle only minutes up the road. There is also a selection of well-regarded schools within walking distance including Loreto NS, Loreto Abbey, Harold's Boys, Castlepark School, Rathdown and St. Joseph of Cluny."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nWelcoming entrance hall with wood effect flooring and useful understairs storage.\n\nLiving Room - \nSpacious reception room to the front featuring carpet flooring, an attractive brick fireplace, coving and a large picture window overlooking the front garden.\n\nDining Room - \nOpen plan to the living room, with carpet flooring, coving and sliding patio doors opening onto the south-facing rear garden.\n\nKitchen Breakfast Room - \nFitted kitchen with a range of wall and floor units, wood-effect flooring and a double bowl stainless steel sink. A window overlooks the rear garden, while the room is plumbed for a washing machine and has provision for a dishwasher. Door to the covered side passage.\n\nGuest w.c. - \nConvenient downstairs guest WC.\n\nGarage - \nAccessible via the covered side passage, providing excellent storage space with potential for a variety of uses.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - \nWith carpet flooring, hot press and access to the attic.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nGenerous double bedroom to the rear with carpet flooring, fitted wardrobes and a large picture window overlooking the garden.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nSpacious double bedroom to the front with carpet flooring, fitted wardrobes and a large picture window.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nGood-sized single bedroom to the front with carpet flooring, fitted wardrobe and window overlooking the front garden.\n\nBathroom - \nFamily bathroom with tiled flooring, partially tiled walls, bath with shower attachment, wash hand basin and window to the rear.\n\nW.C - \nSeparate WC with tiled flooring and window to the rear.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Gas fired central heating </li><li>Exceptionally private south facing garden </li><li>Potential to extend (Subject to PP) </li><li>Short walk to Dalkey town & Dart Station </li><li>Excellent primary and secondary schools</li><li>Converted attic 18sq.m approx.</ul>"
      },
